<section class="think" id="how-we-think" aria-labelledby="think-h2">
  <header class="section-head"><div><p class="kicker">How we think</p><h2 id="think-h2">Advice your team can act on.</h2></div><p>We connect what people already do across support, product, community and partnerships with the decisions and responsibilities needed to help them.</p></header>
  <ol class="principles" id="principles">
    <li class="principle" data-reveal>
      <svg class="principle-mark" viewBox="0 0 96 96" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle class="pm-fill g-c" cx="30" cy="52" r="14"/><circle class="pm-line" cx="62" cy="36" r="10"/><circle class="pm-line" cx="66" cy="72" r="8"/><path class="pm-line" d="M42 46 54 40M40 60 58 68"/></svg>
      <span class="p-idx">01</span>
      <h3>Start with people, not a platform</h3>
      <p>We look at the people using your products or services, building on them, helping peers or bringing others in. Their relationships often cross support, product, community and partner teams.</p>
      <p>We look at what people are trying to do and where they get stuck. Sometimes the answer is a better handoff or clearer documentation. Sometimes it is a useful connection or a focused community programme.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="principle" data-reveal>
      <svg class="principle-mark" viewBox="0 0 96 96" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle class="pm-line" cx="44" cy="44" r="28"/><circle class="pm-line" cx="44" cy="44" r="14"/><circle class="pm-fill" cx="44" cy="44" r="5"/><path class="pm-line" d="m64 64 20 20"/></svg>
      <span class="p-idx">02</span>
      <h3>Understand before committing</h3>
      <p>We investigate needs and behaviour before recommending an approach. That can mean a programme design, different incentives, clearer coordination or stopping an initiative altogether.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="principle" data-reveal>
      <svg class="principle-mark" viewBox="0 0 96 96" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect class="pm-line" x="14" y="30" width="36" height="36"/><rect class="pm-act" x="50" y="30" width="36" height="36"/><path class="pm-line" d="M32 30V14h36v16"/></svg>
      <span class="p-idx">03</span>
      <h3>Make ownership clear</h3>
      <p>Recommendations need people who can carry them forward. We plan the responsibilities, capacity and handovers your team needs to run the approach.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="principle" data-reveal>
      <svg class="principle-mark" viewBox="0 0 96 96" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path class="pm-line" d="M48 12 84 76H12Z"/><path class="pm-fill g-t" d="M48 44 62 70H34Z"/><circle class="pm-fill" cx="48" cy="30" r="4"/></svg>
      <span class="p-idx">04</span>
      <h3>Use AI for a practical purpose</h3>
      <p>We use AI where it speeds up analysis or helps people find knowledge and get a task done. We judge it against the problem at hand, and a person always owns the recommendation.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <aside class="think-proof" aria-labelledby="proof-title" data-reveal>
    <p class="proof-label" id="proof-title">Principle 02 in practice</p>
    <p>In a pre-registered pilot, we asked ChatGPT matched technical questions about Zendesk and Freshdesk and traced every citation. Across three Zendesk answers, every citation came from official documentation and support pages. In the matched Freshdesk answer, 9 of 15 came from hosted community threads.</p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/public-thinking/#research">Follow the research <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </aside>
